BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (Advances are disbursed only after the full travel request has been approved. Employees are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (responsible for settling any outstanding advances before submitting new expense claims.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 728.0 Td (Unsettled advances will block the processing of future reimbursements until the previous) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 713.5 Td (balance is cleared. Any unused portion of the advance must be returned to the finance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 699.0 Td (department within five business days of returning from the trip.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 656.9 Td (Expense Claims) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 627.9 Td (All expenses incurred during business travel must be documented and submitted for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 613.4 Td (reimbursement through the company's digital platform. Expense claims must be submitted in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 598.9 Td (the KestrelHR portal within 30 days of returning; receipts are required for every item above) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 584.4 Td (INR 500. Claims submitted after this deadline will not be processed unless accompanied by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 569.9 Td (valid explanation for the delay, approved by the department head.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 540.9 Td (Receipts must be original, legible, and clearly show the date, vendor name, items purchased,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 526.4 Td (and total amount paid. Digital receipts are acceptable if they meet these criteria. For) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 511.9 Td (expenses below INR 500, a detailed log entry in the portal is sufficient, but employees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 497.4 Td (should retain physical or digital proof of purchase for audit purposes. All claims must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 482.9 Td (categorized correctly \(e.g., accommodation, meals, transport\) to facilitate accurate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 468.4 Td (accounting and budget tracking.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 426.4 Td (Approvals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 397.4 Td (The approval workflow for expense claims is tiered based on the total value of the claim to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 382.9 Td (ensure appropriate oversight. Approval of claims: the line manager approves claims up to INR) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 368.4 Td (50,000; claims above INR 50,000 also need the department head. The line manager is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 353.9 Td (responsible for verifying that the expenses were incurred for legitimate business purposes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 339.4 Td (and comply with this policy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 310.4 Td (The department head reviews high-value claims to ensure alignment with departmental budgets) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 295.9 Td (and strategic objectives. Both approvers must verify that all necessary receipts are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 281.4 Td (attached and that the claim form is complete. Any discrepancies, missing documentation, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 266.9 Td (policy violations identified during the review process will result in the rejection of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 252.4 Td (claim until rectified. Repeated non-compliance may lead to revocation of travel privileges.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 210.3 Td (Personal Vehicle Use) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 181.3 Td (In situations where public transportation or rental cars are unavailable or impractical,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 166.8 Td (employees may use their personal vehicles for business travel. To ensure fairness and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 152.3 Td (accountability, the company reimburses mileage at a standardized rate rather than actual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 137.8 Td (fuel and maintenance costs. Use of a personal car for business is reimbursed at INR 12 per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 123.3 Td (km.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 94.3 Td (Employees must record the starting point, destination, and total kilometers traveled in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 79.8 Td (their expense claim. The route taken should be the most direct and efficient path between) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (Kestrel Shipmanagement \(fictional company\) - FIN-POL-04 v2.0 - page 3 of 4) Tj ET
